  "level": 1,
  "question": {
    "text": "3 moles of mono-atomic gas $(\\gamma=5 / 3)$ is mixed with 1 mole of a diatomic gas $(\\gamma=7 / 3) .$ The value of $\\gamma$ for the mixture will be",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "k6arW",
      "text": "$\\frac{9}{11}$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "bC3nX",
      "text": "$\\frac{11}{7}$",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "IjFR4",
      "text": "$\\frac{12}{7}$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "MCXBx",
      "text": "$\\frac{15}{7}$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "The number of degrees of ireedom for the mixture is\r\n$\\therefore$$\\begin{aligned} f_{\\text {mix }} &=\\frac{n_{1} f_{1}+n_{2} f_{2}}{n_{1}+n_{2}} \\\\ &=\\frac{3 \\times 3+1 \\times 5}{4}=\\frac{7}{2} \\\\ \\gamma &=1+\\frac{2}{f} \\end{aligned}$\r\n$\\Rightarrow \\quad \\gamma=1+\\frac{4}{7}=\\frac{11}{7}$",
    "image": null
  },
